<table><tr><td valign="top">[[File:Everfrost Peaks Ruins.jpg|alt=Everfrost Peaks tundra area.|thumb|Everfrost Peaks, view of the "tundra" area.]]'''Everfrost Peaks''' is a permanently frozen area of frequent snowfalls and constant snow cover. It is the northernmost zone and borders the home of the barbarians, Halas. It is also adjacent to the gnoll home of Blackburrow, where all must pass if they want to enter the lands surrounding Qeynos. It's also connected to Permafrost, a higher-level dungeon to the east. Everfrost can be safely divided into two subzones, the "canyons" and the "plains". 

The "canyons" represent Halas barbarian's newbie area. They are a twisting, maze-like area of dead ends, high ridges, and very few open areas through which the lower-level monsters move. This is also where the entrances to Halas (north) and Blackburrow (south) lay. 

The "plains" are a much more dangerous and vast area. They lie to the east of the "canyons" and stretch on for quite a way before ending in the mountains that contain the entrance to Permafrost. A Y-shaped, frozen river divides the "plains" into eastern and western halves, and ruins of an ancient civilization are scattered throughout the region. </td></tr></table>
